A red city bus arrives.
I board the bus.
There are not many people on the bus.
A woman is sitting near the door.
She smiles.
I need to get to the metro station.
I ask her.
"Hello, does this bus go to the metro station?"
"Yes, it goes there," she says.
"Thank you," I say.
There is an empty seat near her.
I sit in that seat.
The bus moves forward.
I look outside.
I need to alight at the metro station.
